              'prior-consent requirement, but requires accurate headers, a non-deceptive subject, ad identification, a physical address '
              'and an opt-out honoured within 10 business days. Under UK PECR, corporate subscribers can generally receive unsolicited '
              'email, while sole traders and some partnerships are treated as individuals and generally need consent or soft opt-in. '
              'Identity and a valid opt-out apply to both, and UK GDPR still governs personal data. Sources: '
              'https://www.ftc.gov/business-guidance/resources/can-spam-act-compliance-guide-business and '
              'https://ico.org.uk/for-organisations/direct-marketing-and-privacy-and-electronic-communications/business-to-business-marketing/',
              '<b>Instagram is a platform permission, not a legal safe harbour.</b> Meta’s spam policy prohibits deceptive or overwhelming '
              'behaviour, and its Prohibited Commercial Practices policy allows restrictions, feature limits or account disablement for '
              'deceptive commercial conduct. Meta does not publish a rule saying a cold sales DM is automatically welcome. Send one '
